@{
    ViewBag.Title = "SAML setup";
}

<h1>SAML setup</h1>
<p>POC #2 is waiting for the Entra tenant values from the office email. Replace <code>YOUR-TENANT-ID</code> in <code>SmalAuth.Saml\Web.config</code>.</p>

<dl>
    <dt>SP Entity ID</dt>
    <dd>@SmalAuth.Saml.SamlSettings.SpEntityId</dd>
    <dt>ACS URL</dt>
    <dd>@SmalAuth.Saml.SamlSettings.AcsUrl</dd>
    <dt>Federation metadata</dt>
    <dd>@SmalAuth.Saml.SamlSettings.MetadataUrl</dd>
    <dt>Tenant ID</dt>
    <dd>@SmalAuth.Saml.SamlSettings.TenantId</dd>
</dl>

<p>Register the Entity ID and ACS URL on the Entra Enterprise Application, then open a protected URL such as <a href="@Url.Action("Edit", "Customer", new { id = 12345 })">/Customer/Edit/12345</a>. That path is stored in RelayState and restored after the assertion is validated.</p>
<p>RSA is not part of this spike.</p>
